@*
    The Zazi mark, the same shape the handset draws.

    Two bars and the stroke that joins them. The upper bar sits left, the lower one right,
    because the product's whole job is reconciling two sides that do not line up, and the
    diagonal is what brings them together. It reads as a Z without being a letter dropped
    into a circle.

    The geometry is ZaziBrand.kt's, multiplied by 100: the Kotlin expresses it as fractions
    of the canvas (bar 0.20, shift 0.12) so one path serves a 24dp mark and a launcher icon,
    and the same fractions serve any size here. Keep the two in step — an agent who sees the
    handset and the portal in the same afternoon should see one product.

    Inline SVG rather than an image file: it recolours with the theme through currentColor,
    stays crisp at any size, and costs no request. Solid fill only — there is no gradient
    anywhere in the identity.

    aria-hidden because it is decoration wherever it appears; the wordmark beside it carries
    the name, so announcing the shape as well would say "Zazi" twice.
*@

<svg class="mark @Class"
     viewBox="0 0 100 100"
     width="@Size" height="@Size"
     fill="currentColor"
     aria-hidden="true"
     focusable="false">
    <path d="M0,0 L88,0 L88,20 L30,80 L100,80 L100,100 L12,100 L12,80 L70,20 L0,20 Z" />
</svg>

@code {
    /// <summary>Rendered size in pixels, square.</summary>
    [Parameter] public int Size { get; set; } = 22;

    /// <summary>Extra classes, for the rare case a page needs to position it.</summary>
    [Parameter] public string? Class { get; set; }
}
